' A 3D node in VBR (Godot slice 9) — a spinning cube.
'
' 3D is the same surface as 2D: a different base class (`Node3D`, `CharacterBody3D`,
' Camera3D…) and 3-component vectors. The property/method passthrough is identical,
' so `Me.Rotation`, `Me.Position`, `Me.LookAt(…)` all just work.
'
' `vbr rungodot examples/godot_3d.vbr` generates a 3D starter scene (a box mesh, a
' camera, a light). For a real game, build your own scene in the Godot editor.

Node3D "Spinner"
    Export Speed As Single = 1.0

    On Ready
        Debug.Print "3D spinner ready"
    End Ready

    On Process(delta)
        ' Spin around the Y axis (rotation is a Vector3 of euler angles, radians).
        Me.Rotation = Me.Rotation + Vector3(0, Speed * delta, 0)
    End Process
End Node3D
